attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a long spine.** Columns 0 to 28, `rpmD` to `yhdV`, are carried by 94 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 1% of calls {S1, P}. The model names 89 to 100% of them, fewest at column 24, `yhdZ`, 89% {S1}.

@variable **A short variable stretch follows**, columns 29 to 31, `acrF` to `acrS`, carried by 86 to 90%, [[multidrug efflux]] {S2, Q}. Then a second spine, columns 32 to 65, `yhdU` to `sspB`, carried by 92 to 97%, [[rod shape-determining]] at columns 43 to 45 {S3, Q}. Through columns 74 to 78 a branch of 5 shell families runs in 29 to 32%, [[fimbrial biogenesis]] {S6.b74, X}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 98 against 91%, and hesitates less there, 0.11 against 0.35 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 30, `acrE`, a variable column, 0.64 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork columns.** Columns 71 to 79, `nanK` to `mtgA`, are carried by 30 to 90%, the stretch most in regions of plasticity, 5 to 35% {S6, P}. The last column is `mtgA`, in 30% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 97% of genes**, 0.15 bits on average, perplexity 1.2 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.80 against 0.11 bits, and names fewer genes, 70% against 98% {C}.

